<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Francisco Sabino Vieira</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1797–1846</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Francisco Sabino Vieira was a doctor and journalist in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salvador">Salvador</a> who led the rising of November 1837 that proclaimed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bahia">Bahia</a> Republic, a revolt known after him as the Sabinada. The rebels held Salvador until imperial forces retook it in March 1838 after bloody street fighting. Sabino was exiled to the interior of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>, where he died.</p></div>
